{"annotations":{"destructiveHint":false,"idempotentHint":false,"openWorldHint":true,"readOnlyHint":false},"description":"Run any AI model on Wiro. Supports image, video, text, audio, 3D, and more. Call `get_model_schema` first. With `wait=true` this performs a bounded wait; when the response contains `nextAction.tool = \"wait_for_task\"`, call that tool with the exact arguments returned. Do not resubmit the original request. A completed tool-call turn instead returns a `run_model` continuation template; execute its calls, fill its `toolOutputs`, and invoke it once. When the task completes, present every returned media resource in the user-facing response instead of reporting only task metadata.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"https://json-schema.org/draft/2020-12/schema","additionalProperties":false,"properties":{"model":{"description":"Model slug in \"owner/model\" format, e.g. \"google/veo3-1\", \"google/nano-banana-pro\"","type":"string"},"params":{"additionalProperties":{},"description":"Model-specific parameters as key-value pairs. Use get_model_schema to discover available parameters. Pass json and json-array parameters as structured JSON values in this same object. File parameters take public URLs, no upload needed: one URL for fileinput, an array of URLs for combinefileinput, and for multifileinput the URLs comma-separated in its matching ...UrlMultiple field. A parameter you leave out gets the default get_model_schema shows for it. A run fills nothing for the ones it marks as samples (file fields, ids that contain \"input\", the prompt and the LLM chat fields), picks a random seed, and refuses a required parameter that is missing. To continue a chat, send the same session_id with the next prompt, without previousTaskToken. A turn that ended with tool calls is continued with previousTaskToken, toolOutputs rows (call_id and output) and the same session_id, as its nextAction shows.","propertyNames":{"type":"string"},"type":"o